  "service": "Vertex AI Agent Builder",
  "title": "Discovery Engine: Per-Feature Access Policies & `verification` Field Now Read-Only",
  "summary": "A breaking change makes the `verification` field in `EngineFeaturePolicyMember` read-only. Additionally, Discovery Engine now supports granular per-feature access policies on `Engine` resources, allowing you to control which users or groups can utilize specific engine features.",
  "details": "The `verification` property within the `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMember` schema (and its `v1alpha`/`v1` counterparts) has been made read-only. If your code previously attempted to write to this field, it will now encounter errors and must be updated to reflect its immutable nature. This is a breaking change. On the new capabilities front, `Engine` resources (across `v1`, `v1alpha`, and `v1beta`) now expose a `featurePolicies` map. This new property allows you to define `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicy` objects for individual features, specifying `allowedMembers` and `deniedMembers` (of type `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMember`) to precisely control access. You can also set a `defaultAccess` (ALLOW/DENY) for users not explicitly listed. This enables fine-grained management of who can use particular engine functionalities.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
